Tournament Analysis
  vertices: sheaf sites
  observable: restriction residual defects, side-chart load, union-only sections, full covers, apex-lift full covers
  switch: harder = more residual, then more side-chart load
  fingerprints={'score_hist': {0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1}, 'directed_3_cycles': 0, 'sccs': [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1], 'hardness_order': ['one_lift_all_slack', 'Vstar_slack', 'first_open_gap_slack', 'AP_slack', 'zero_slack_control', 'double3_control']}

Synthesis
  The denominator-14 apex chart is large but not complete: side charts
  are needed for lifted full covers.  The useful object is therefore a
  certificate sheaf, not one global apex witness.  In this bounded site,
  every full restriction is certified by a cheap section; restriction
  residuals are zero.  A few two-lift rows are union-only: each one-lift
  restriction is a ledger failure, while the two-lift union creates a full
  cover with a cheap witness.  That is exactly the local-to-global behavior
  the next HYP-2099/HYP-2100 bridge lemma should formalize.
